{
  "number": 434,
  "title": "We Speak of the Realms",
  "key": "F",
  "time": "4/4",
  "tempo": "Moderato",
  "tune": "",
  "category": "Doctrines",
  "subcategory": "",
  "lyricist": "",
  "composer": "",
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "Verse 1",
      "type": "verse",
      "lines": [
        "[F]We speak of the realms of the blest,",
        "[Bb]That [F]country so bright and so [C]fair,",
        "[F]And oft are its glories confessed-",
        "[Bb]But [F]what must it [C]be to be [F]there!",
        "[F]We speak of its pathway of [Bb]gold-",
        "[Bb]Its [F]walls decked with jewels so [C]rare,",
        "[F]Its wonders and pleasures untold-",
        "[Bb]But [F]what must it [C]be to be [F]there!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Verse 2",
      "type": "verse",
      "lines": [
        "[F]We speak of its freedom of sin,",
        "[Bb]From [F]sorrow, temptation [C]and care,",
        "[F]From trials without and within---",
        "[Bb]But what [F]must it [C]be to [F]be there!",
        "[F]We speak of [Bb]its service of love,",
        "[Bb]Of the [F]robes which [C]glorified wear,",
        "[F]Of the church of the First Born above-",
        "[Bb]But what [F]must it [C]be to [F]be there!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Verse 3",
      "type": "verse",
      "lines": [
        "[F]Our mourning is all at an end,",
        "[Bb]When, raised [F]by the [C]life-giving word,",
        "[F]We see the new city descend,",
        "[Bb]Adorned [F]as a [C]bride for [F]her Lord;",
        "[F]The city so [Bb]holy and clean,",
        "[Bb]No sorrow [F]can breathe [C]in the air;",
        "[F]No gloom of affliction or sin,",
        "[Bb]No [F]shadow of [C]evil, [F]is there."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Verse 4",
      "type": "verse",
      "lines": [
        "[F]Do Thou, midst temptation and woe,",
        "[Bb]For [F]heaven my [C]spirit prepare;",
        "[F]And shortly I also so shall know",
        "[Bb]And feel [F]what it [C]is to [F]be there.",
        "[F]Then o'er the bright [Bb]fields we shall roam,",
        "[Bb]In [F]glory celestial [C]and fair,",
        "[F]With saints and with angels at home,",
        "[Bb]And [F]Jesus Himself [C]will [F]be there."
      ]
    }
  ]
}